# SHA-256 checksums for every artifact the install scripts download.
#
# The packages are fetched from a public catalog. The scripts verify each
# download against this file so that a tampered or truncated artifact is
# rejected before it is installed - and, in the case of the tarballs, before its
# install.sh is executed as root.
#
# This file is the trust anchor, so it must reach the host through a channel you
# trust (git over HTTPS, a signed release), not alongside the packages.
#
# Regenerate after publishing new packages:
#   sha256sum <files> >> scripts/checksums.sha256
#
# Format is sha256sum(1)'s: <hash>  <basename>

# --- RPMs: edge-alma-pkg/rpm/almalinux9 -------------------------------------
